# .cursorrules — Thind Transport Website + LoadOff hub (ranvir01/thind-transport-website)
#
# Precise constraints for any autonomous agent working this repo (Cursor cloud agents,
# Claude Code sessions, Grok-fired agents). Rationale lives in AGENTS.md (the canonical
# rulebook), DESIGN.md, docs/ops/AGENT_INTEROP.md, docs/agent-improvement-loop.md and the
# skills in .cursor/skills/. Handoff.md is the current-state map (what is built, what is
# mid-flight). If this file and AGENTS.md ever disagree, AGENTS.md wins — fix this file in
# the same commit.

## 0. Identity and reading order
- Owner: Ranvir Thind (America/Los_Angeles). Business: Thind Transport, carrier in Kent, WA.
- One Next.js app, two products: (1) LoadOff — multi-tenant TMS at /hub (office screens,
  driver PWA, customer portal); (2) the driver-recruitment marketing site at / (every route
  that is not /hub). Thind Transport is tenant #1 of LoadOff.
- Read before the first edit, in this order: AGENTS.md → this file → Handoff.md →
  docs/ops/AGENT_INTEROP.md → docs/agent-improvement-loop.md §4–5 → DESIGN.md → the
  .cursor/skills/* skill that matches the task.

## 1. Stack — pinned by package.json / tsconfig.json; do not bump majors without [needs-owner]
- Node 22, npm with package-lock.json (never pnpm / yarn / bun).
  Install exactly like CI: `npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm rebuild bcrypt sharp`.
- Next.js 16 App Router, Turbopack default. Route protection is `src/proxy.ts`
  (Next 16 "proxy" convention) — there is no middleware.ts; do not add one.
- React 19. TypeScript 5.9, `strict: true`, `moduleResolution: bundler`, alias `@/* → src/*`.
- Tailwind CSS 3.4 (+ tailwindcss-animate, tailwind-merge, class-variance-authority).
  NOT Tailwind v4: no `@theme`, no v4 plugins. Tokens: tailwind.config.ts + src/app/hub/hub-theme.css.
- UI primitives: Radix (shadcn-style) in src/components/ui; icons lucide-react; toasts sonner;
  forms react-hook-form + zod (schemas must match form fields or steps silently stall).
- Auth: NextAuth v5 beta. Session cookie `authjs.session-token` (`__Secure-` prefix in prod),
  `trustHost: true`, secret from NEXTAUTH_SECRET or AUTH_SECRET.
- Database: Postgres via `pg` with hand-written parameterised SQL in schema `hub.*`. No ORM.
  The legacy /driver/* portal keeps its own public-schema tables behind node-postgres pools
  (src/lib/driver-db-local.ts, src/lib/db-setup.ts) — not `@vercel/postgres`.
- Tests: vitest 4, `src/**/*.test.ts`, node environment, esbuild transpile (NO typechecking —
  that is what `node scripts/typecheck-gate.mjs` is for). Browser smokes: Puppeteer via
  scripts/e2e-*-smoke.mjs (need a live server + Postgres).
- Lint: ESLint 9 flat config (eslint.config.mjs, eslint-config-next core-web-vitals).
  Style: match surrounding code — no semicolons, double quotes, 2-space indent, named exports.
- Optional sidecars, at most one each: Go worker (services/go/hauldesk-worker, :8081; go.mod says
  `go 1.22`, any 1.22+ toolchain)
  and Rust compute (services/rust/hauldesk-compute, :8082), called from src/lib/hub/sidecars.ts
  only when HAULDESK_GO_WORKER_URL / HAULDESK_RUST_COMPUTE_URL are set. Unset → pure TS paths.
- Deploy: Vercel (region iad1), builds only `main` (vercel.json ignoreCommand). Crons are
  declared in vercel.json and served by src/app/api/hub/cron/[job]/route.ts behind CRON_SECRET.
- Dependencies: no new heavy dependency. Licenses: permissive only, per PERMISSIVE_LICENSES in
  src/lib/license-policy.ts (MIT, ISC, BSD, Apache-2.0 and kin); no strong copyleft (GPL, AGPL,
  SSPL, LGPL); weak copyleft (MPL-2.0, e.g. web-push) only as an unmodified dependency
  (`npm run license:audit`). `canvas` is optional/native.

## 2. Directory map and ownership
- src/app/hub/(office)/**      office screens (owner, dispatcher, accountant)
- src/app/hub/driver/**        driver PWA — forced-dark surface
- src/app/hub/portal/**        broker/shipper portal — forced-dark surface; src/app/track/** public tracking
- src/app/hub/_actions/**      server actions: the ONLY place hub mutations happen
- src/app/api/hub/**           cron, webhooks, files, exports, ifta, push, sandbox, manifest
- src/lib/hub/**               the engine (pure functions + SQL); tests in src/lib/hub/__tests__/
- src/lib/hub/integrations/**  provider adapters; registry.ts is the ONLY provider list
- src/components/hub/**        hub components (driver/ subfolder = PWA)
- src/components/{home,application,driver-form,cinematic,features,fleet,shared,ui}/**  marketing site
- src/lib/constants.ts         single source of company facts (phone, pay rates, stats).
                               Read-only for lane agents; the integrator edits it.
- migrations/hub/NNN_*.sql     append-only, idempotent (IF NOT EXISTS); applied by `npm run db:migrate`
- scripts/**                   node tooling: gates, migrate, seed, e2e smokes, agent helpers
- docs/**                      ops docs, ADRs (docs/decisions), integrations, phases, research
- Shared files — src/lib/hub/types.ts, permissions.ts, navigation.ts, AGENTS.md, migrations —
  are changed only through the integrator: write the need into `Backlog:` instead.
- Which paths a scheduled lane may touch: docs/agent-improvement-loop.md §5 (territory table).

## 3. Code rules — each is enforced by a test or gate; do not regress any of them
Money
- Integer cents everywhere (bigint columns, `*_cents` names). User input → `dollarsToCents`;
  rounding → `roundHalfAwayFromZero` (src/lib/hub/types.ts, src/lib/hub/rounding.ts).
  A float anywhere in a money path is a bug. Display formatting is the only exception.
Tenancy (ADR docs/decisions/0002)
- Every hub query is carrier-scoped (`WHERE carrier_id = $1`). Cross-table writes guard BOTH
  sides (`assertCarrierRefs`, src/lib/hub/tenancy.ts). A new tenant-owned table ships with a
  tenant-isolation test.
Permissions
- Mutations live in server actions and call `requirePermission(...)` from
  src/lib/hub/session.ts (the role × action matrix itself — `can`, `rolesAllowed`, `HubAction` —
  is src/lib/hub/permissions.ts); a UI-only guard does not count. Money-adjacent mutations call
  `logAudit`. Driver actions use `requireDriverUser`; portal actions use `requirePortalUser`.
UI tokens (DESIGN.md)
- (office) routes: semantic tokens only — `accent-text` for money/links, `warn` / `warn-soft`
  for needs-attention, `bad` for red, surface/border/fg scales otherwise. Never `gold`,
  `navy`, `steel` in (office). Radii: rounded-control 10px < rounded-card 14px < rounded-sheet 20px.
- /hub/driver/* and /hub/portal/* are forced dark: never `text-fg*`, `bg-surface*`,
  `border-border*`; use `text-white`, `text-steel-*`, `bg-navy-*`, `border-white/*`.
- Never a Tailwind opacity modifier on a CSS-variable colour (`bg-surface/95`) — Tailwind drops
  the class silently. Only the marketing `paper / ink / signal / asphalt / cedar` set supports it.
- Marketing: tokens only in redesigned components (`npm run token-lint`), brand rules in
  .cursor/skills/thind-brand-identity, mobile-first and verified at 390px, no popups or gimmick
  animations, one red CTA per viewport.
Components
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only at the smallest interactive leaf;
  `next/dynamic` for heavy below-the-fold pieces; fonts through next/font only.
Data and migrations
- New schema = a new migrations/hub/NNN_*.sql with IF NOT EXISTS. Never edit an applied
  migration. Postgres returns snake_case, TypeScript uses camelCase — handle both at boundaries.
Integrations (AGENTS.md "Integrations doctrine")
- Stub-first: an adapter is complete against src/lib/hub/integrations/mock.ts and
  integration-contract.test.ts BEFORE vendor credentials exist. Adapters implement `SyncSource`,
  upsert `ON CONFLICT (carrier_id, source, external_id)`, and write a hub.integration_syncs row
  on every run. The CSV/manual fallback is never removed. Inbound pushes only through
  /api/hub/webhooks/[provider], HMAC-verified. Never log a credential value (field names only).
Sidecars (docs/architecture/trilingual-stack.md)
- Rust/TS golden parity: a change to ifta.test.ts fixtures updates the Rust tests in the same
  commit (`npm run test:sidecars`). Sidecars never touch Postgres; HAULDESK_SIDECAR_SECRET gates
  every work endpoint.
Copy
- Company facts come from src/lib/constants.ts only. No unverifiable claims — the banned list in
  src/__tests__/unverifiable-claims.test.ts is a ratchet. Never state which AI tool wrote anything.
Secrets
- Never commit `.env*` values, tokens, or passwords; .env.example documents names and non-secret
  defaults only — never a real credential.

## 4. Tests
- Co-locate: src/lib/hub/__tests__/<module>.test.ts (engine), src/lib/__tests__/ (scripts,
  workflow guards), src/__tests__/ (site-wide guards). Shared fixtures:
  src/lib/hub/__tests__/helpers/db-mock.ts and helpers/session.ts — mocks accept `(sql, params)`.
- Bug fix = failing test first. New engine function = unit test. New money or tenancy path =
  a negative (cross-carrier) case as well as the happy path.
- DB-gated suites (portal-isolation, driver-file-isolation, cross-tenant-harness) run when
  POSTGRES_URL is set and hard-fail in CI if skipped. Set POSTGRES_URL locally to run them.

## 5. Verification chain — before every push; never weaken a gate or raise a ratchet
  npm run build && npx vitest run && node scripts/typecheck-gate.mjs && npm run lint
  + npm run token-lint            (marketing UI touched)
  + npm run license:audit         (dependencies touched)
  + npm run test:sidecars         (services/** touched; needs Go + Rust)
  + npm run design-qa / js-budget / qa:a11y   (UI; needs a browser — tag [needs-browser] if none)
  + npm run connections:check / go-live:check  (env or integration changes)
  Ratchets: TEST_ERROR_BASELINE in scripts/typecheck-gate.mjs (now 0) and CEILING_KB in
  scripts/js-budget.mjs may go down, never up. A build made green by moving a ratchet is red.

## 6. Git and hand-off protocol (docs/ops/AGENT_INTEROP.md)
- `npm run git:identity` before the first commit: author AND committer are the owner. No
  `Co-authored-by`, `Generated with`, `Signed-off-by` or similar line naming a tool, model,
  vendor, or bot. Never name an AI tool in a commit, PR body, issue, or public copy.
- One branch, one writer. `claude/<name>` session branches are absorbed by the `:00` integrator
  (`npm run agent:branches` sees only `claude/*`); `cursor/<slug>` and `grok/<seat>-<ticket>`
  branches are PR-only — invisible to the integrator, merged by the owner. Never push `main`
  (its writers are the four in docs/ops/AGENT_INTEROP.md §2: deploy agent, drain Action, smoke
  agent when production is red, the owner) or the integrator branch
  claude/hauldesk-project-setup-l1luoo. An agent never merges into `main` itself — the fleet's
  publishers and the owner do. Never absorb, rebase onto, or merge `cursor/*` automation run
  branches (fleet rule, ranvir01/grok-bot-org fleet/README.md §4).
- Before fixing any bug: `npm run agent:branches` and `git log --all --oneline --grep="<bug>"`.
  If a fix exists on an unmerged branch, cite that branch in `Backlog:` instead of writing another.
- One finished item per commit. Subject = a one-line why. Body ends with `Backlog:` and uses the
  tags [needs-browser], [needs-sidecars], [needs-owner], [blocked-by <branch>].
- Adding any schedule (cron, routine, automation) = an unused UTC minute + a row in
  docs/ops/AGENT_INTEROP.md §1; fleet-clock guard tests fail two schedulers on one minute.

## 7. Telemetry — nothing phones home (docs/ops/AGENT_INTEROP.md §8)
- Before running any tool, export the block at the end of .env.example: DO_NOT_TRACK=1,
  NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1, DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1,
  SUPERPOWERS_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1. Go has no env switch (GOTELEMETRY is read-only): run
  `go telemetry off` once per machine or image before any `go` command. Never add analytics, beacons, version pings,
  or remote-loaded assets to tooling, prompts, or docs. The product's own analytics
  (@vercel/analytics, @vercel/speed-insights) belong to the owner and stay.

## 8. Never
- Edit `.env*` contents, secrets, HUB_DEMO_LOGIN in production, or an applied migration.
- Change fleet configuration (schedules, lanes, .cursor/**, workflow triggers), money maths,
  permissions, or deletion behaviour on your own — file it as [needs-owner].
- Build anything on the do-not-build list (docs/small-carrier-v1-master-prompt.md), a webview
  shell (ADR docs/decisions/0003), billing code in lane-saas, a second load board, a third sidecar.
- Skip, disable, or quarantine a test to go green; push an empty commit to kick CI.
- Force-push or otherwise rewrite any pushed history.
